(7486109, 1191256, 59029, '<td valign="top">Woohoo!!  Congrats on a great pic Marcel - fantastic use of white space and the sardine can key in particular.  Very well done and executed, and Coach Susan is very proud of you too :-)</td>', 'Woohoo!!  Congrats on a great pic Marcel - fantastic use of white space and the sardine can key in particular.  Very well done and executed, and Coach Susan is very proud of you too :-)', '2016-12-07 07:43:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486111, 1191363, 104230, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the ribbon sweetie, and on the perseverance in turning round after you got home and going back there for a second time ;-)</td>', 'Congratulations on the ribbon sweetie, and on the perseverance in turning round after you got home and going back there for a second time ;-)', '2016-12-07 08:50:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486122, 1191256, 142473, '<td valign="top">Personally, I like the left half of the image much better than the whole thing.  I''m not a fan of the rolled paper and sardine can tab.  That half doesn''t mean anything to anyone other than maybe just being "clever".  It looks like you just wanted to fit a theme.  Taken out of this challenge context, I think this image falls flat - there would be no hope of a viewer "getting it".  The left side of the image could at least be viewed as emulating mountains or a river or something.  The right half is just "why"?  Don''t take this wrong, I appreciate the creativity, I just didn''t see it the same way everyone else apparently did.  Figured even blue ribbons need a little dissenting opinion from time to time to help them grow.  Cheers.</td>', 'Personally, I like the left half of the image much better than the whole thing.  I''m not a fan of the rolled paper and sardine can tab.  That half doesn''t mean anything to anyone other than maybe just being "clever".  It looks like you just wanted to fit a theme.  Taken out of this challenge context, I think this image falls flat - there would be no hope of a viewer "getting it".  The left side of the image could at least be viewed as emulating mountains or a river or something.  The right half is just "why"?  Don''t take this wrong, I appreciate the creativity, I just didn''t see it the same way everyone else apparently did.  Figured even blue ribbons need a little dissenting opinion from time to time to help them grow.  Cheers.', '2016-12-07 11:25:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486123, 1191244, 142473, '<td valign="top">Love what you found here.</td>', 'Love what you found here.', '2016-12-07 11:26:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486156, 1191399, 19825, '<td valign="top">This finished higher in my ranking. Nice shot.</td>', 'This finished higher in my ranking. Nice shot.', '2016-12-07 17:02:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486157, 1191393, 103032, '<td valign="top">Aaah, I should have guessed it was yours.  I love these shots.  It was my top pick.</td>', 'Aaah, I should have guessed it was yours.  I love these shots.  It was my top pick.', '2016-12-07 17:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486239, 1191363, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyClick:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on the ribbon sweetie, and on the perseverance in turning round after you got home and going back there for a second time ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yah, if it weren''t for Penny I''d have been dead in the water (or out of it, actually): I''d forgotten it was minimal editing for this challenge, and I shot this on the last day of the challenge; we''d had nothing but grey skies for the previous week or so. Anyway I walked in the door saying "Got it!" and she looked up with concern in her eyes and said "You DID remember it was Minimal, right?" Of course, I hadn''t taken my phone with me so I couldn''t receive her text :-(I turned around without a word and went back out to my car. Love you, Sweetie!</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyClick: Congratulations on the ribbon sweetie, and on the perseverance in turning round after you got home and going back there for a second time ;-)  Yah, if it weren''t for Penny I''d have been dead in the water (or out of it, actually): I''d forgotten it was minimal editing for this challenge, and I shot this on the last day of the challenge; we''d had nothing but grey skies for the previous week or so. Anyway I walked in the door saying "Got it!" and she looked up with concern in her eyes and said "You DID remember it was Minimal, right?" Of course, I hadn''t taken my phone with me so I couldn''t receive her text :-(I turned around without a word and went back out to my car. Love you, Sweetie!', '2016-12-07 20:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486383, 1191194, 100831, '<td valign="top">Congrats Deb... love the angles.</td>', 'Congrats Deb... love the angles.', '2016-12-08 09:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
